<p>Early tenants included Merchants National Bank. Business offices later occupied the ground floor, and a community church moved into the former billiards room.</p>

<p>In July 1985, {% person "ben-hanna" %}Ben{% endperson %} and {% person "dan-hanna" %}Dan Hanna{% endperson %} sold the building to Lewis and Clark Investments, Inc. Its major stockholders included {% person "william-clairmont" %}William Clairmont{% endperson %} of Bismarck, {% person "wallace-joersz" %}Wallace Joersz{% endperson %}, and Dan Hanna of Mandan. Using a $975,000 MIDA bond package, the company converted 67 hotel rooms into 45 rent-subsidized one- and two-bedroom apartments. The lobby was later remodeled, and rear meeting rooms with skylights reopened for public use.</p>
